---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement | Abilene Eye Institute"
  description="Accessibility commitment and features of the Abilene Eye Institute website demonstration."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold text-navy-900">Accessibility statement</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        An eye care practice's website should be usable by people with low vision. This site is
        designed to WCAG 2.2 AA: strong color contrast, large readable text, visible keyboard focus,
        a skip-navigation link, semantic headings, descriptive labels, and support for reduced-motion
        preferences.
      </p>
      <p>
        The self-assessment and all navigation work with a keyboard alone and with screen readers.
        No information on this site is conveyed by color alone, and no text is baked into images.
      </p>
      <p>
        If any part of this site is difficult to use with assistive technology, please tell the
        office so it can be corrected. Known limitations are documented in the project's
        accessibility notes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
